  "construction_notes": [
    {
      "text": "From the state Housing Element Annual Progress Report, through 2025.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001099",
        "SRC-001107"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC CA-25-638: Berryessa TOD, located at 1565 Mabury Road in San Jose on a 0.8 acre site, requested and is being recommended for a reservation of $5,698,379 in annual federal tax credits and $82,584,672 of tax-exempt bond cap to finance the new construction of 195 units of housing, consisting of 193 restricted rental units and 2 unrestricted manager's units.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001666"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City of San Jose permit MP23-006 (Ministerial Permit, folder year 2023), status Approved, issue date 2025-02-12: \"SB 35 Ministerial Permit to allow the construction of a 10-story, 100 percent affordable housing development consisting of 195 units, including 2 manager units, on a 0.79-net-acre site located in the Berryessa BART Urban Village. The project includes 8 c\" (city text cut off at 255 characters)",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001956"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "VTA presentation (2026-04-07) names the project RISE, the first phase of a three-phase development on the VTA-owned lot; future phases are conceptualized as market-rate apartments on Parcel C and market-rate office on Parcel A, with Parcel D built out as an access road and landscaping. HA Builder Group, LLC presented as contractor. Construction schedule: ground improvement and foundation May-July 2026; structural concrete July 2026-June 2027.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002646"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Affirmed Housing release (2026-06-02): built on land leased from VTA; the City of San Jose, HCD, Destination: Home and the Bay Area Housing Innovation Fund provided public, predevelopment and mezzanine funding; Santa Clara County Office of Supportive Housing provided capital funding.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002643"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "CTCAC staff report: bond issuer City of San Jose; bond counsel Hawkins, Delafield & Wood LLP; private placement purchaser Citibank, N.A.; general partners AHG Berryessa, LLC and CFAH Housing, LLC (joint venture); parent companies Affirmed Housing Group, Inc. and Compass for Affordable Housing; HUD Section 8 project-based vouchers.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001666"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dahlin Group page: nine residential levels over one story of parking and services; 203,515 sq ft total building area; units 413 to 1,027 sq ft; 2024 Gold Nugget Merit Award, Best On-the-Boards Affordable Housing.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002645"
      ]
    }
  ],
